{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Reliance Segment Revenue Rollup — SUMIFS & Reconciliation",
  "scenario": "Your Mumbai desk maintains raw quarterly segment revenue for Reliance Industries across three divisions (Oil-to-Chemicals, Retail, Digital Services) spanning four fiscal years. You must rebuild the annual summary table using SUMIFS, apply SUBTOTAL to respect filtered views, and reconcile totals against corporate filings.",
  "instructions": "Build SUMIFS formulas to extract annual revenue by segment, apply COUNTIFS to verify data completeness, use SUBTOTAL to total a filtered range, and reconcile your output against the filing total.",
  "learning_objective": "Construct SUMIFS formulas with multiple criteria, apply COUNTIFS to count qualifying rows, use SUBTOTAL to respect filters, and validate segment totals against source data.",
  "hints": [
    "SUMIFS puts the sum range first, then condition pairs in order: sum_range, criteria_range1, criteria1, criteria_range2, criteria2.",
    "To sum Retail revenue for FY25 only, write =SUMIFS(rev_column, segment_column, \"Retail\", year_column, \"FY25\") — exactly two criteria, each a pair.",
    "For the reconciliation check, SUBTOTAL(9, filtered_range) totals only visible rows; compare it to your SUMIFS block total to confirm no hidden data was missed."
  ],
